@using Odyssey.Dtos
@using Odyssey.Dtos.Finance

@*
    OdsTagIconPicker — the tag icon chooser for transaction, journal, task and photo tags (Odyssey Design
    System · components/TagIconPicker).

    A closed grid of the TagIcons catalogue, not a search over the Material set: a tag's
    icon is a key from the fixed list the API validates against, so the picker offers exactly that
    list and nothing the server would refuse. The catalogue is the shared Odyssey.Dtos declaration,
    never a client copy.

    The search box above the grid filters that same catalogue (TagIconSearch: label, keywords and key,
    typo-tolerant). While a query is typed the Default cell is hidden, the grid shows the matches best
    first, and a polite status line announces the count. Arrow Down moves from the box into the grid,
    Enter picks the first match, Escape clears a non-empty query instead of closing the dialog.

    The first cell is always Default — value null, drawn with the generic tag glyph inside a dashed
    outline. DefaultIcon / DefaultLabel / DefaultCaption re-dress that cell for another owner of the same
    catalogue (photo albums, issue #406); their defaults are today's tag strings. The API never stores the default key, so the picker emits null for it, and it treats any
    unknown or stale value as Default, mirroring the server's read-side projection.

    ARIA radiogroup with a roving tab stop: arrows move in two dimensions over the live column count,
    Home/End jump, selection follows focus (the radio pattern); Space/Enter fall to the native click. icon-picker.js keeps those keys from
    scrolling the dialog and reports the column count. The caption names the selection in words and
    previews the label of the cell under the pointer or focus, so meaning never rests on the glyph.

    The cells are 48px with 24px glyphs and the grid scrolls inside a seven-row window; icon-picker.js
    scrolls the selected cell into that window on attach, and arrow-key focus keeps it there.

    Keys render only as text inside a material-icons span — never MarkupString, never a class or style
    fragment (issue #279 security review).
*@

<div class="@RootClass">
    <div class="odc-iconpick-search">
        <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">search</span>
        <input type="search" class="odc-iconpick-search-input" @ref="_search"
               placeholder="@SearchLabel" aria-label="@SearchLabel" aria-controls="@_groupId"
               maxlength="@TagIcons.MaxKeyLength" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" disabled="@Disabled"
               value="@_query" @oninput="OnQueryInput" @onkeydown="OnSearchKeyDownAsync" />
    </div>
    <div class="odc-iconpick-grid" role="radiogroup" id="@_groupId"
         aria-label="@(AriaLabelledBy is null ? AriaLabel : null)" aria-labelledby="@AriaLabelledBy"
         aria-describedby="@AriaDescribedBy"
         aria-invalid="@(Invalid ? "true" : null)"
         @ref="_grid" @onmouseleave="OnGridMouseLeave">
        @for (var i = 0; i < _visible.Count; i++)
        {
            var index = i;
            var cell = _visible[index];
            var active = index == SelectedIndex;
            var isDefault = cell.Key is null;
            <button type="button" role="radio" data-idx="@index"
                    @key="@(cell.Key ?? "__default")"
                    @ref="_buttons[index]"
                    aria-checked="@(active ? "true" : "false")"
                    aria-label="@(isDefault ? DefaultLabel : cell.Label)"
                    disabled="@Disabled"
                    tabindex="@(index == TabStopIndex ? 0 : -1)"
                    class="@CellClass(active, isDefault)"
                    @onclick="() => PickAsync(index)"
                    @onkeydown="e => OnKeyDownAsync(e, index)"
                    @onmouseenter="() => _peek = index"
                    @onfocus="() => OnCellFocus(index)"
                    @onblur="OnCellBlur">
                <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">@(cell.Key ?? DefaultIcon)</span>
                @if (active)
                {
                    <span class="odc-iconpick-check" aria-hidden="true"><span class="material-icons">check</span></span>
                }
            </button>
        }
    </div>
    @if (_visible.Count == 0)
    {
        @* Outside the radiogroup, and aria-hidden: the status line already announces it. *@
        <div class="odc-iconpick-empty" aria-hidden="true">No icons match “@_query”.</div>
    }
    <div class="odc-sr-only" role="status">@StatusText</div>
    <div class="odc-iconpick-caption" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="odc-iconpick-sel">
            <span class="material-icons">@(Selected.Key ?? DefaultIcon)</span>
            <span>@(Selected.Key is null ? "Default" : Selected.Label)</span>
            @if (Selected.Key is null)
            {
                <span class="odc-iconpick-sub">@DefaultCaption</span>
            }
        </span>
        @if (Peeked is { } peeked)
        {
            <span class="odc-iconpick-peek">
                <span class="material-icons">@(peeked.Key ?? DefaultIcon)</span>
                <span>@(peeked.Key is null ? "Default" : peeked.Label)</span>
            </span>
        }
    </div>
</div>
